   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Department of the Treasury</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Banking &amp; Financial Services - Seychelles</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to assist the GoS in developing and maintaining a fair, safe, and stable financial sector that benefits and protects financial sector participants while maintaining public confidence in the financial system and supporting private sector-led economic growth. Project components will focus on: (1) implementing a new core banking system to facilitate centralized operational processes within the CBS; (2) strengthening the capacity of CBS banking supervision staff to adequately regulate and supervise the banking sector; (3) establishing a deposit insurance regime that protects depositors in the event of bank failures and maintains public confidence in the financial sector; (4) developing and implementing an effective resolution framework that allows for the orderly resolution of failed financial institutions; and (5) developing an automated data portal for inbound financial institution reporting to support enhanced offsite analysis of financial institution risks.</narrative>
  </description>
